# Vulnerabilities the image scans (ci.yml, scripts/pre-deploy-check.ps1) accept for now, in every image. Each entry
# says why, and expires (exp:) so it is looked at again: after that date the scan fails on it until it is fixed or
# deliberately extended. Ones that apply to one image only are in docker/trivy/<image>.trivyignore instead, so they
# can't hide the same ID in another image.

# Silo RELEASE.2026-10-18T00-00-00Z (silo and mcli) is built with Go 1.27.2; crypto/x509 is fixed in 1.27.3, and no
# Silo release has it yet. In this stack Silo and mc only talk plain HTTP inside the compose network, so no
# certificate is ever checked. Take the next Silo release that is built with a fixed Go.
# Caddy 2.11.7 (Go 1.26.8) has it too: there it would only affect Caddy's own outbound calls (the certificate authority),
# which already go to a fixed address over TLS it verifies. Take the next Caddy release (docker/trivy/caddy.trivyignore).
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-21
